# PXA Overdrive -- draft preset for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (PXQN2) on two V100s
#
# Model : the Flash-Next PXQN2 file
# Cards : 2x Tesla V100 16 GB (sm_70) + system RAM
#
# UNMEASURED DRAFT (W1, 2026-10-11). Same rows as the 1x V100 draft.
# The only serving difference is two visible cards and a layer split.
# Tensor split is a later arm (W5), not this file.
#
# Since 2026-10-19 the Overdrive switch set is not written out in this file: the engine applies it itself at
# startup (PXA_AUTO_OVERDRIVE, on by default) when it reads this class out of the model file and the file is larger
# than the cards. The set and the decision that applies it live in the PXQN library, so on a build without that
# library nothing is applied. This file carries the one line that forces the set (PXA_OVERDRIVE=1), the box rows
# an operator may have to adjust, and the site rows. PXA_NO_OVERDRIVE=1 turns the set off; a value you export for
# any one switch is kept. The set the engine applies is the frozen-residency recipe E (2x V100 +3.9% / +8.1%
# over the earlier preset arm, 2026-10-14).
#
# Node 0 is CPUs 0-17 and 36-53. The pool stays on 0-17. CPUs 18-35 and
# 54-71 are node 1 and are not used.
#
# The expert map is the learned one beside the model file, else the per-user
# cache. This preset does not hardcode a path.

# --- Overdrive: the engine applies the measured switch set for this class; =1 forces it even on cards the file
# would fit (the class itself must match; a tensor split still stands it down), =0 turns it off like PXA_NO_OVERDRIVE=1 ---
PXA_OVERDRIVE=1

# --- box ---
# Node 0 only. Unmeasured arms, not selected: 0-15, and 0-17,36-53.
PXA_XCACHE_CPUPOOL_CPUS=0-17
PXA_NUMA_BIND=1

# --- site ---
# Pinned host memory is off. Delete this line to test pinning on. Unmeasured.
GGML_CUDA_NO_PINNED=1
PXA_PLE_MMAP=2
CUDA_DEVICE_ORDER=PCI_BUS_ID

# PXA_PXQN_V70_N3_VERIFY_I8 stays unset until it is measured on this MoE file.

# --- server arguments (draft, not timed) ---
#   -ot 'per_layer_token_embd\.weight=CPU' -ngl 99 -fa on -np 1 -t 18 --jinja
#   --no-context-shift --cache-ram 0 -c 16384 -ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0
#   --spec-type mtp:n_max=4,p_min=0.75 -sm layer
# Show the process exactly two V100s. Do not use -sm tensor with this draft.
